</p><p><font    color="#FFFFF5">When it was done, he put the pen aside.     ally    chimpanzee       The wind, only the wind.</font></p><p><font     color="#FFFFF5">This knowledge did not bring fear but a sense of resignation — he had needed the medication, and he had somehow managed to escape his room and get it.   No curlicues.  "Nothing wrong with the idea, either,»he said.     ""Maybe. the terminally ill.    Perhaps all he had hated was the fact that her face on the dust jackets had overshadowed his in his author photographs, not allowing the critics to see that they were dealing with a young Mailer or Cheever here — that they were dealing with a heavyweight here.      He had half-expected another period of deep depression or rage to follow, but none had.     barefaced</font></p>
