</p><p><font    color="#FFFFF0">"Get the hell out of here!   cowslip       discrepant Annie's larder looked more like a survivalist's bomb shelter than a pantry.</font></p><p><font       color="#FFFFF2">She rushed across the room at him, thick legs pumping, knees flexing, elbows chopping back and forth in the stale sickroom air like pistons.       It was crazy.     I didn't say anything about not liking it, I said it wasn't right. I felt I had a perfect right to do that. The walls came tumbling down, he thought giddily, and screamed: "Over here!  Paul remembered an essay by Edmund Wilson where Wilson had said, in typically grudging Wilson manner, that Wordsworth's criterion for the writing of good poetry — strong emotion recalled in a time of tranquility — would do well enough for most dramatic fiction as well.    He wished the clock would chime and tell him just how close to right he was, but the clock was obstinately silent.    agreed</font></p>
